<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28232" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόχμιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>across, aslant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόχμια . . ἦλθον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.116
				</span></i>
			, cf. E <i><span class="en">
				<u>Or.</u>
				1261
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. κέλευθον ἐμβάνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1000
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				575
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέσε δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1169
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Prosody, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποὺς δ.</span>”
				<i>the dochmiac measure,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Choerob.
					<u>in Heph.</u>
					p.219
				</span></i>
			 C.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυθμὸς δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.Quint.
					1.17
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Bacch.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				100
			</span></i>:—hence Adj. forms, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχμιᾰκός</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Aristid.Quint.
			</span></i> l. c.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχμικός</span></b> ,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχ-αϊκός</span></b> , Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				128
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				937
			</span></i>. (Perh. cf. Skt. <i>jihmá-</i>
		'oblique'.)</div>
